cat at the bottom of the stone, indicating that there was likely no third line.",{"_":54,"ana":55,"ref":56},"chiselled","#execution.chiselled","http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1",{"lettering":58,"dimensions":59},"Large, precise, and tall letters. Serifs used on all letters.",[60,66,72],{"type":61,"l":62,"from":63,"to":63,"h":64,"unit":65},"letterHeight","Line 1","line1","at least 29","mm",{"type":61,"l":67,"from":68,"to":68,"h":69,"unit":65,"atLeast":70,"atMost":71},"Line 2","line2","46-48","46","48",{"type":73,"l":74,"from":63,"to":68,"unit":65},"interlinear","Interlineation line 1 to 2",{"_":76,"notBefore":77,"notAfter":78,"evidence":79},"First or second century CE",1,200,"lettering",[81,87],{"_":82,"type":83,"ref":84,"cert":85,"region":86},"Thermae Himeraeae","ancient","http://pleiades.stoa.org/places/462513","low","Sicilia",{"_":88,"type":89,"ref":90,"region":86},"Termini Imerese","modern","http://sws.geonames.org/6539140",[92],[93,94],37.98365,13.69555,{"_":96,"type":97,"subtype":98,"geo":20},"The place, date, and circumstances of the discovery are unknown, but the inscription is assumed to come from Termini Imerese","found","discovered",[],{"_":101,"type":102,"subtype":103,"when":104,"resp":105,"xml:id":106,"geo":20},"Antoniou, 2023-07-07. In the Depositi of Museo Civico Baldassare Romano, room 1, scaffold 13, shelf 3","observed","autopsied","2023-07-07","#AA","autopsy",[108,115],{"n":109,"url":110,"height":111,"width":112,"desc":113,"surfaceType":114},"screen","ISic000254_tiled.tif","3680px","5520px","I.Sicily with the permission of the Assessorato Regionale dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana - Dipartimento dei Beni Culturali e dell’Identità Siciliana; photo J. Prag 2023-07-07","front",{"n":109,"url":116,"height":111,"width":112,"desc":113,"surfaceType":117},"ISic000254_rear_tiled.tif","rear","Sicily",{"_":120,"role":121,"ref":122,"museum":123},"Museo Civico Baldassare Romano","museum","http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/museum/066",{"slug":124,"type":121,"name":120,"uri":122,"description":125,"location":126},"066","A large and well-displayed collection. It begins with three ante-rooms, in the first of which is a rich display of lithics (mainly Neolithic) from the surrounding area. A display of material from Himera (lion-head spouts from the Temple of Victory and red-figure craters being the principle pieces) and a numismatic gallery then follow before the main room which contains Hellenistic and Roman material from Termini Imerese itself. Small finds, sculpture and inscriptions predominate. The museum collection continues upstairs with non-archaeological material (and a single inscription). The courtyard of the building holds a large collection of architectural pieces and inscriptions",{"settlement":88,"region":127,"country":128,"address":129,"geo":130},"Palermo","Italy","Via Marco Tullio Cicerone, 90018 - Termini Imerese (PA)",{"lat":131,"lon":132},37.98655109,13.69587845,{"_":134,"type":135},"25","inventory",{"_":137,"mainLang":138,"languages":139},"Latin","la",[137],{"type":141,"bibl":142},"edition",[143,153],{"type":144,"n":145,"author":146,"date":147,"citedRange":148,"ptr":149,"ref":151,"inscriptionDate":147,"year":38},"corpus","ILMusTermini","Bivona","1994","180",{"target":150},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/JCV85C79",{"_":152,"target":152},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002137",{"author":146,"date":154,"citedRange":155,"ptr":156,"ref":158,"inscriptionDate":154,"title":160,"citation":161,"uri":162,"year":163},"1975-1976","556 no.25 tav.11",{"target":157},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/3JCJI9JF",{"_":159,"target":159},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002140","Nuove iscrizioni di Termini Imerese (Palermo)","\u003Cspan>Livia Bivona, «Nuove iscrizioni di Termini Imerese (Palermo)», \u003Ci>Atti della Accademia di Scienze, Lettere a Arti di Palermo\u003C/i> Ser.4, 35, fasc. 2 (1976 1975): 531–58\u003C/span>","https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/3JCJI